# {{display}}

Scaffolded by `nmp init {{name}}`.

## Composition is a library (ADR-0046)

`crates/{{pkg}}` is a **thin composition shell** over the NMP framework. Its
`register` function inherits the canonical NMP composition with one call to
`nmp_defaults::register_defaults` — the Bevy-`DefaultPlugins` /
Spring-Boot-starter pattern. There is no generated FFI crate: you depend on the
framework's default composition, you do not generate it.

## Layout

| Path | What |
|------|------|
| `nmp.toml` | NMP dependency policy (read by `nmp doctor` / `nmp upgrade`). |
| `crates/{{pkg}}/src/lib.rs` | The composition shell: `register` → `register_defaults`, plus an example app-owned domain (`EntryRecord`). **App nouns never go in `nmp-core`** (doctrine D0). |
| `crates/{{pkg}}/examples/shell.rs` | Headless shell: `NmpAppBuilder` → `register` → `start`. |

## Build and run

```sh
cargo check                              # the {{pkg}} shell compiles as-is
cargo test -p {{pkg}}                    # shell tests pass
cargo run --example shell -p {{pkg}}     # build → app-core register → start
```

## NMP dependency modes

The scaffold pins NMP one of two ways (see `crates/{{pkg}}/Cargo.toml`):

* **local checkout** (default / `nmp init … --nmp-path DIR`) — `path = …`
  dependencies into an NMP checkout, for framework development.
* **release** (`nmp init … --nmp-version X.Y.Z`) — git-rev pins on
  `github.com/pablof7z/nostr-multi-platform` at tag `vX.Y.Z`. External
  consumers pin NMP by git rev; see `docs/architecture/external-consumers.md`
  in the NMP repo.

## Upgrade NMP

```sh
nmp upgrade --to 0.4.0    # bump the pinned rev + rewrite nmp-* deps
nmp doctor                # confirm the dependency policy
```

